==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Coined in 1912 by Swiss psychiatrist [[w:Paul Bleuler|Paul Bleuler]] (1857-1939) from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|autismus|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|αὐτός||self|tr=autos|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{clinical psychology}} [[biological|Bio-]][[neurological]] [[disorder]] that is observable in early [[childhood]] with symptoms of abnormal [[self-absorption]], characterised by lack of [[response]] to other humans and by limited ability or disinclination to [[communicate]] and [[socialize]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|clinical psychology}} [[mindblindness]], [[on the spectrum]] {{qualifier|slang}}

====Derived terms====
* [[autistic]], [[autism spectrum disorder]], [[on the spectrum]]

